      },
      "summary": "The implementation records the requested investigation lifecycle and trace events. The redaction test does not cover leakage of the citation quote value under a different field name.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/InvestigationTraceRecorderTests.cs",
          "line": 224,
          "message": "AC TRACE-PRODUCER-02 does not verify that the citation quote value is absent from the serialized trace; add a distinct quote sentinel and assert it is absent.",
          "confidence": 0.93,
          "category": "other",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The trace redaction assertions check the full model response and the property name \"quote\", but never check a distinct sentinel for the citation quote value.",
            "failureScenario": "If a future trace stores only the citation quote under another property name, these assertions still pass, despite TRACE-PRODUCER-02 requiring the serialized trace to contain none of the quote sentinel values."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
      "reviewType": "testing",
      "harness": "codex",
      "harnessVersion": "0.162.0",
      "model": "gpt-6-luna",
      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The production investigation path and acceptance tests cover the main lifecycle. Model supplied tool names are persisted unchecked, which can place prohibited prompt or document text in a trace.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Investigation/BoundedInvestigator.cs",
          "line": 322,
          "message": "Validate tool names against the known tool set before recording them, or record only a fixed categorical identifier; model supplied tool names can carry prohibited content into persisted traces.",
          "confidence": 0.87,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The model response’s FunctionCallContent.Name is passed directly to the trace recorder before FunctionInvokingChatClient validates or executes the tool call. The recorder stores it as InvestigationTraceStep.ToolName, and the execution service appends that trace even when tool execution fails.",
            "failureScenario": "If a model response contains an unknown tool call whose name includes prompt or document text, the recorder stores that text in the trace before the call fails. The trace then violates AC TRACE-PRODUCER-02’s prohibition on storing prompts, model responses, and raw document text. OWASP LLM02:2025 Sensitive Information Disclosure."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "security-reviewer",
      "reviewType": "security",
